  "subject": "🐕 Axios Finish Line: How dogs read us",
  "date": "Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:29:21 -0400",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🏃 Plus: Sunlit trail | Wednesday, September 16, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n PRESENTED BY AMERICA’S CREDIT UNIONS \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Sep 16, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 279 words … 1 min. Copy edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: How dogs read us \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Annelise Capossela/Axios\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n New research is providing evidence for what pet owners and animal lovers have long suspected: Dogs are remarkably good at reading human emotions.\n\n Why it matters: The findings offer clues about how living as human companions for thousands of years may have shaped dogs. 🧠 Zoom in: For the study, published recently in iScience , researchers scanned pups' brains while they looked at photos of human facial expressions portraying a range of feelings, including happiness, fear, sadness and anger.\n\n Dogs processed the faces just like humans do, focusing on eyes, noses and mouths, and their brains showed a distinct response to happy faces. While smiles elicited the biggest response, dogs appeared to read the other emotions, too. And their brains didn't put all the negative feelings in the same bucket.\n\n Instead, brain activity differed depending on whether the pups were looking at a fearful, sad or angry face. 🔎 The intrigue: This study analyzed dogs' brain responses when they were looking at photos of strangers.\n\n Their reactions would likely be even stronger when observing their owners' faces, the study authors note. 💛 The money quote: \"Humans are really good at picking up small details on the face, and so are dogs,\" study author Raúl Hernández-Pérez from the University of Vienna told the BBC .\n\n The bottom line: Whether it's your dog or one you meet out and about, you're not the only one getting something out of saying hello.\n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM AMERICA’S CREDIT UNIONS\r\n\n \r\n Turning financial opportunity into stability \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Bringing financial opportunity to families and economic stability to the nation.\n\n\r\n For generations, credit unions have helped families turn hard work into lasting stability, offering low-cost loans, expanding financial access and providing a path to economic freedom.\n\n\r\n Learn more. \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 🌳 New lingo: &quot;Greenbath&quot; \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Josh Trent Pic du jour from reader Josh Trent in Cheverly, Md.:\n\n \"Fantastic morning 'greenbath' as the sun peeks through on the running trail.\" \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;